<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40487" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπέτομαι</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πτήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.15
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεπτάμην</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-όμην</span> (v. infr.); later, also in act. form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέπτην</span>, part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπτάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.407
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Nicarch.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				1.25
			</span></i>:—<i>fly to</i> or <i>towards</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθ᾽</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅμιλον ἐπιπτέσθαι μενεαίνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.126
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ . . ἐπέπτατο δεξιὸς ὄρνις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					13.821
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. σοὶ τωὐτὸ ὄνειρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.15
				</span></i>
			;
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾗ ᾽πέπτετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					48
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀετὸς ἐπιπτόμενος</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					2.4.19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. c.acc.,
				<i>fly over</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεδία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1486
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆν καὶ θάλατταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					118
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἀρούραις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					17.16
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καινὰ καὶ θάυμαστὰ
			ἐ</span>. <i>fly over to, run eagerly after</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1471
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ πάντα τὰ λεγόμενα
				ὥσπερ ἐπιπτόμενοι</span>
			<i>flitting</i> from one to another, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				365a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>. <i>fly
			at</i> or <i>on to</i>, of a male bird, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				564b4
			</span></i>.</div>
